1
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Postman Pat: The Movie is a family, comedy,
animation film directed by Mike Disa.

2
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:54,000
Like always, Postman Pat is happily going about his duty delivering
letters and parcels around the fictional town of Greendale.

3
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:18,000
One day, auditions for the TV talent show, "You're the One", are
held in Greendale, which Pat manages to pass.

4
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:42,000
With Pat required to be away from Greendale whilst participating in the contest,
various Patbot 3000 robots are deployed to take Pat's postal duties.

5
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:06,000
This soon turns out to be an evil plot to take over
the world, which Pat must now stop.

6
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:30,000
Postman Pat (voice), played by Stephen Mangan.

7
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:54,000
CEO (voice), played by Jim Broadbent.

8
00:35:12,000 --> 00:35:18,000
Josh (voice), played by Rupert Grint.

9
00:39:36,000 --> 00:39:42,000
Wilf (voice), played by David Tennant.

10
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
Postman Pat (singing voice), played by Ronan Keating.

11
00:48:24,000 --> 00:48:30,000
Sara Clifton (voice), played by Susan Duerden.

12
00:52:48,000 --> 00:52:54,000
Postman Pat: The Movie is a 2014 animated comedy film based on the British
television series Postman Pat by John Cunliffe and Ivor Wood.

13
00:57:12,000 --> 00:57:18,000
It was directed by Mike Disa, produced by Robert Anich Cole, written by
Nicole Dubuc, with music by Rupert Gregson-Williams.

14
01:01:36,000 --> 01:01:42,000
It was co-produced by Classic Media, RGH Pictures and Timeless Films.

15
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
The film stars Stephen Mangan, Jim Broadbent, Rupert Grint, David Tennant, Ronan
Keating, Susan Duerden, Sandra Teles, TJ Ramini and Peter Woodward.

16
01:10:24,000 --> 01:10:30,000
It was released in the UK on 23 May 2014 by Lionsgate UK and Icon
Film Distribution respectively and in the US by Shout!

17
01:14:48,000 --> 01:14:54,000
Factory, and received mixed reviews from critics.

18
01:19:12,000 --> 01:19:18,000
The film grossed $8.6 million worldwide.

19
01:23:36,000 --> 01:23:42,000
The tone is lighthearted.
